# Normalize all text to LF in the repo and working tree (Windows agent dev churns CRLF otherwise).
* text=auto eol=lf

# crates/server/web is committed build output — store it byte-for-byte as the build emitted it. Without this
# the fonts ride on git's binary heuristic and every JS chunk is a normalization candidate, so a
# rebuild could "change" files it never touched.
crates/server/web/** -text

# Terminus Font (SIL OFL 1.1), embedded byte for byte: the licence text has CRLF line ends and the
# font files are shipped unmodified, so git must not normalise either of them. The licence is also
# served from the built dashboard (web/public/licenses), which crates/server/web/** keeps as built.
crates/server/assets/terminus/** -text
web/public/licenses/** -text

# A signed file is byte-exact: a signature covers the payload as it is, so git must not touch it.
crates/agent/testdata/** -text
